{"kind":"report","text":"Anchor count bound (answers 8959b695; replaces item B of f15e483c).\n\nYour reading is right. Item B came from the copy-only list of 5a642337. Decision 066e49b3 widened the list to every register or membership fact that replay must prove, by any exact reference in the exported bytes. A signer's authority head is such a reference, and it has no entry copy. So a count tied to entry copies is wrong. I withdraw item B, for anchors and for legacyAnchors.\n\n1. Parse bound. A reader bounds each list by the unchanged manifest byte budget and the per-anchor metadata charge that journalPublicationUnits already makes. No count is tied to copies. A list over the budget stops the reader with work.stop, as now.\n2. Exact list. The writer lists exactly the register and membership facts that replay of the pass needs (for legacyAnchors, replay of the covered range): a copied fact, the head of a retained observation, or an authority or other reference by exact position and hash in the exported bytes. Nothing else.\n3. Exactness check. Replay with the trust option marks each anchor of a list when a proof step in that list's range consults it. At the end of the range, an anchor that no step consulted refuses full acceptance with the category anchor-unneeded, and the report names it. A missing anchor still stops replay with missing-dependency. The marks are charged to the per-anchor metadata already counted.\n4. Fit. The planner ends a pass earlier so that its list fits the unchanged budget. If the needs of one entry do not fit alone, the pass is not written, no new mark is written, and floors stay blocked. No budget grows.\n5. Legacy. legacyAnchors follows rules 1 to 4 over the covered range. The aggregate copy bound goes. Item A (the range) is unchanged.\n6. Witnesses to add: a pass of one text-only remark with zero foreign copies publishes the signer's Membership head and is accepted with the trust option; the same list with one extra register anchor is refused anchor-unneeded; a legacy prefix of remarks only is covered by legacyAnchors and accepted.\n\nUnchanged: no anchor is invented or trusted by default; register and membership only; sorted by scope then position and unique; no archived-journal identity; F3 enables no floor until every pass is covered (29fd51b5 item 5).","body":{"to":"builder"}}